  "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation Analysis\n\n## Task Requirements\nThe task required:\n1. Finding a blog identifying the top-10 trending travel destinations for 2026\n2. Determining how many of them are in Asia\n\n## Screenshot Analysis\n\n**Screenshot 1:** Shows the blog \"Top 10 Trending Travel Destinations 2026 Worldwide\" on tickyourlist (published January 30, 2026), confirming the correct blog was located. The list begins with \"1. Madeira, Portugal.\"\n\n**Screenshot 4:** Shows destinations #2 (Tbilisi, Georgia — explicitly described by the blog as \"the next big cultural hotspot in Europe\"), #3 (Chicago, United States), #4 (Quy Nhon, Vietnam), and #5 (Puerto Escondido, Mexico).\n\n**Screenshots 3 & 5:** Show #7 (Glasgow, United Kingdom), #8 (Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates), and #9 (Recife, Brazil).\n\n**Screenshot 2:** A full-page thumbnail confirming the complete numbered list structure of 10 destinations.\n\n## Response Verification\n\nThe response states: \"2 of the top-10 trending travel destinations for 2026 are in Asia: Quy Nhon, Vietnam and Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates.\"\n\nChecking this against the visible evidence:\n- **Quy Nhon, Vietnam (#4)** — Southeast Asia ✓ Correctly identified as Asian\n- **Abu Dhabi, UAE (#8)** — Western Asia ✓ Correctly identified as Asian\n- **Tbilisi, Georgia (#2)** — The blog itself frames it as European, so excluding it is consistent with the source\n- Other visible destinations (Madeira, Chicago, Puerto Escondido, Glasgow, Recife) are clearly not Asian\n\nThe count of 2 is consistent with the screenshots, and no visible screenshot contradicts this claim. The response directly answers the question posed in the instruction.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**SUCCESS**",
